    <h2 class="sr-only">About</h2>

    <div class="about-body reveal">
      <p>
        I'm an AI/ML engineer with research and production experience. At
        <strong>Wiley</strong>, I work on building and evaluating AI-powered applications
        that deliver knowledge from scholarly and educational content. My work spans
        retrieval systems, evaluation frameworks used across Wiley's RAG products,
        content generation, and applied ML for publishing, with a through-line of
        grounding AI in trusted domain sources.
      </p>
      <p>
        I build systems end to end, and I care a lot about evaluation. The interesting
        part of shipping a retrieval or generation system isn't the first working
        prototype; it's the harness around it that tells you honestly whether a change
        helped or hurt. Q&amp;A benchmarks at collection scale, LLM-as-judge layered over
        strict matching, sweeping the retrieval configuration space before anything
        touches production. The kinds of things that keep the rest of the work honest.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before Wiley I did an MS in CS at Stanford (AI track) and a BS in Electrical
        Engineering at UCSD. My research has spanned robot simulation (iGibson 2.0 at
        CoRL 2021), bioelectronics (wireless smart bandages, Nature Biotechnology), and
        deep learning for general aviation. On the side I'm working on an independent
        project on outcome switching in clinical trials, a paper in progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
